;; Reviewed 2026-10-08 (written by Claude, from the design, the MACRO
;; manual, the VAX's listing and the debugger runs; for the user's
;; review). Why this is right:
;; - COPY(x, v) with x or v longer than 65535 characters, LOCC's and
;;   MOVC5's most, is done in pieces (decided with the user 2026-10-08):
;;   m, the most characters it may copy, is LEN(v) - 1, or LEN(x) if
;;   less. LOCC #0 searches at most 65535 bytes at a time from R1, R2 the
;;   bytes left; it leaves R1 at the 0X when it finds one (Z clear) or past
;;   the piece (MACRO 9-130), so R1 less x's address is n, the characters
;;   to copy, pushed on the stack. MOVC3 then moves at most 65535 of them
;;   at a time, from where the last left R1 and R3 (MACRO 9-132), the count
;;   left on the stack as MOVC3 overwrites R0-R5; CLRB (R3) puts the 0X
;;   after the last, and the rest of v is left as it was.
;; - The runs find the 0X in the second piece (69000), the first (10) and
;;   not at all (70000, all of x), and copy into mid, which takes 65999,
;;   and small, 9, and through CopyTo's VAR parameter, @4(AP). EXAMINE
;;   shows an offset above 65535 as an address, not a symbol.
;; - A string constant still takes one MOVC5, as in vax-copy.
; VaxCopyLong, written by poc (doc/developer/vax-macro32-backend.md)
	.TITLE	VAXCOPYLONG
	.IDENT	/65e054de0ccc5401/
	.PSECT	POC_CODE,  PIC,SHR,NOWRT,EXE,LONG
